WEBVTT

00:29.290 --> 00:30.580
It targeted itself?!

00:41.290 --> 00:43.930
This is bad! I'll self-destruct the missile!

00:45.070 --> 00:46.030
Don't touch it!

00:46.610 --> 00:48.310
B- But!

00:55.900 --> 00:58.570
Yukikaze will sooner destroy itself...

00:59.410 --> 01:03.520
...then let them capture us!

01:04.020 --> 01:05.290
You're serious?!

01:28.380 --> 01:31.060
Battle Fairy

01:28.380 --> 01:31.060
YUKIKAZE

01:29.730 --> 01:31.730
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

02:23.540 --> 02:24.950
Rei...

02:32.550 --> 02:33.630
I'm here.

02:33.630 --> 02:38.320
<i>Major, the general's waiting. Can you please come to the control room?</i>

02:38.320 --> 02:41.350
Right, understood. I'm on my way.

02:54.240 --> 02:58.650
Mission objective, unknown.
His readings are terribly unstable.

02:59.640 --> 03:02.480
As though he's confused and frightened...

03:04.050 --> 03:07.500
Mode VC. Voice confirmation.

03:08.420 --> 03:11.180
Announcement from Lieutenant Fukai to unit B-3.

03:11.520 --> 03:14.080
Maintain current data processing.

03:14.380 --> 03:16.260
Stand by in combat mode.

03:16.260 --> 03:17.600
Prepare for enemy attack.

03:21.300 --> 03:24.030
This is a clear operation.

03:25.800 --> 03:28.220
Don't worry, Yukikaze.

03:52.490 --> 03:55.670
What's keeping those two?!

03:56.360 --> 03:58.270
For God's sake...

03:58.270 --> 04:01.240
Sorry for keeping you all waiting.

04:01.240 --> 04:04.430
Lieutenant General Laitume. Major General Linneberg.

04:04.970 --> 04:07.440
It's not a problem, Brigadier General.

04:07.440 --> 04:10.610
I do find this an unusual idea.

04:10.610 --> 04:12.660
Still...

04:13.180 --> 04:19.790
Is there any purpose to bringing us all here like this?

04:19.790 --> 04:21.940
Yes, of course there is.

04:22.490 --> 04:26.510
Gentlemen, this is an excellent opportunity for us...

04:26.510 --> 04:33.460
...to carefully listen to the thoughts of the supreme commander of the FAF and the general chief of the intelligence forces.

04:34.400 --> 04:36.460
Our thoughts?

04:36.940 --> 04:42.460
Yes, sir. For example, the matter you've assigned to Rombert.

04:42.940 --> 04:45.970
The mutiny of the corps we just retrained!

04:53.190 --> 04:54.710
System down.

05:00.130 --> 05:02.030
Sorry we're late.

05:03.570 --> 05:08.900
It's true we gave approval with foreknowledge of his actions.

05:09.740 --> 05:14.700
However, the one who was complicit in it... was myself.

05:15.110 --> 05:16.920
You, General?!

05:17.280 --> 05:19.130
Why?

05:26.590 --> 05:28.800
For the intelligence.

05:29.890 --> 05:34.810
Rombert wanted to become a JAM.

05:35.600 --> 05:40.900
By means of betrayal, a truly human method.

06:46.200 --> 06:50.800
We still believe we minimized casualties in this.

06:50.800 --> 06:55.000
Wait, then the reason you gathered all of the copies into one unit...

06:55.580 --> 06:59.340
was to let Rombert start a mutiny?!

08:01.980 --> 08:06.070
To learn more about an enemy, you infiltrate them.

08:06.920 --> 08:10.840
It's a common practice in an intelligence war.

08:11.120 --> 08:12.590
So, then...

08:13.420 --> 08:16.800
That's why the JAM created copies of humans!

08:17.360 --> 08:19.660
To infiltrate...

08:19.660 --> 08:22.640
You copied their tactics!

08:36.040 --> 08:38.410
Do you understand now?

08:39.380 --> 08:41.910
What your methods have led to?

08:42.080 --> 08:45.210
You've invited disaster to us!

08:46.150 --> 08:49.760
Even so, we had to know for sure.

08:49.760 --> 08:52.710
What the JAM truly are.

08:53.460 --> 08:56.810
Will that be all, Brigadier?

08:56.900 --> 09:00.930
It looks like it's time we finished this.

09:02.070 --> 09:05.390
Lieutenant, give the orders to B-3.

09:06.810 --> 09:09.240
Lt. Fukai to Yukikaze.

09:09.340 --> 09:12.280
Moving to mission phase two.

09:13.080 --> 09:15.410
Cut processing on the designated data.

09:16.420 --> 09:19.230
Avoid damage and remain on stand by.

09:46.780 --> 09:52.940
We have the SAF to thank for pulling off this little stunt.

09:52.950 --> 09:55.820
I appreciate it, Brigadier.

09:56.390 --> 09:58.320
No need to thank me, sir.

09:58.320 --> 10:02.950
I decided it was the best plan to ensure our survival.

10:05.380 --> 10:10.960
That "best plan" being a complete withdrawal to Earth...

10:12.210 --> 10:14.840
<i>B-2, Chunyan to Banshee 3.</i>

10:14.840 --> 10:16.980
<i>Have brought General Laitume and others.</i>

10:16.980 --> 10:19.250
<i>Requesting landing clearance.</i>

10:19.270 --> 10:22.270
<i>Banshee 3 to Chunyan. You are cleared to land.</i>

11:23.310 --> 11:26.910
They've taken the dummy data we're sending as bait.

11:27.120 --> 11:29.910
But for how long?

11:31.090 --> 11:33.920
It's bought us enough time.

11:34.360 --> 11:37.080
The evacuation of our personnel is going smoothly.

11:38.830 --> 11:42.160
But B-3 had to be left behind...

11:42.860 --> 11:47.180
It has to finish this.

11:48.070 --> 11:51.250
Right, okay. I'll be counting on you.

11:52.140 --> 11:53.440
Worried?

11:54.640 --> 11:55.930
No problem.

12:43.090 --> 12:46.150
I knew Rombert for a long time.

12:46.330 --> 12:51.160
I think I know him better than anyone else.

12:51.160 --> 12:55.620
Even so, why did he?

12:56.200 --> 13:01.770
Because gathering intelligence was his way of fighting this war.

13:44.890 --> 13:46.650
Channel, open!

13:46.650 --> 13:49.480
B-3 is engaging them in the underground residential area.

13:50.390 --> 13:53.470
Move the operation to phase three.

13:54.300 --> 13:56.850
A mop-up battle...

15:08.490 --> 15:11.220
I see...

15:12.600 --> 15:14.550
So, that's what they did...

15:18.450 --> 15:22.970
Such a simple thing... Why didn't I figure it out?

15:26.950 --> 15:28.290
What's wrong?

15:28.290 --> 15:29.920
It's picked up a signal.

15:31.930 --> 15:33.160
A transmission?

15:35.000 --> 15:38.790
<i>All of you, continue the fight.</i>

15:40.540 --> 15:46.370
<i>The JAM are on an eternal quest for knowledge of all things.</i>

15:46.380 --> 15:50.010
<i>While they have not yet satisfied their desire to understand you,</i>

15:50.550 --> 15:54.040
<i>you can stand against them.</i>

15:57.290 --> 16:01.780
<i>This has never been a war between the JAM and humanity.</i>

16:04.530 --> 16:12.070
<i>Everything, now and in the future, goes according to the JAM's calculations.</i>

16:12.090 --> 16:16.910
<i>This is a model equation, merely an experiment to confirm their theories.</i>

16:24.310 --> 16:27.340
Which means that we...

16:34.290 --> 16:37.600
...must do what we can to upset that equation.

16:41.760 --> 16:46.930
I don't know how long we can stay ahead of the JAM's predictions...

16:49.400 --> 16:52.620
But, while we can...

16:54.310 --> 16:57.530
...the war will never end.

16:58.550 --> 17:02.810
Humanity can survive!

17:05.020 --> 17:10.090
<i>That is all. This is the final report of Ansel Rombert,</i>

17:10.090 --> 17:14.290
<i>commander of the intelligence corps, analysis division. Signing off.</i>

17:26.070 --> 17:29.670
The price you pay for the time you live...

17:30.380 --> 17:33.760
...is a never ending battle!

17:40.820 --> 17:44.120
That... is the answer!

17:54.890 --> 17:56.700
B-3...

17:58.940 --> 18:00.600
Target, locked.

18:01.240 --> 18:03.040
On approach.

18:03.040 --> 18:06.780
Wait! But, he's still...

18:08.940 --> 18:10.250
That's right.

18:15.690 --> 18:19.090
He's still... human.

18:34.710 --> 18:38.010
<i>Pandora 1, this is Banshee 3. Cleared to land.</i>

18:38.010 --> 18:43.280
<i>Roger, Pandora 1. Check. Guide beacon, received. Catch arm, locked.</i>

18:44.240 --> 18:46.290
<i>Pandora 1, following the flight deck crew.</i>

18:46.290 --> 18:49.230
<i>Roger, Pandora 1.</i>

18:49.460 --> 18:51.890
<i>Now receiving final flight from Troll base.</i>

18:51.890 --> 18:56.230
<i>Crew are to follow instructions to portside blocks B through E.</i>

18:56.430 --> 19:03.260
372TFS, maintain current altitude
until we finish receiving 321SAS.

18:57.330 --> 19:03.260
Unit 128TAS holding,
requests refueling.
Send the tanker in
that area over to them.

19:03.800 --> 19:07.910
We've situated a necessary number of nuclear devices within the power point.

19:07.910 --> 19:13.250
Once we pass, we'll detonate them, destroying the dimensional passageway.

19:14.550 --> 19:16.740
Nothing will be left behind.

19:16.950 --> 19:18.590
That would mean...

19:18.590 --> 19:24.780
It's a plan the high command have considered repeatedly.

19:25.390 --> 19:28.290
For decades in fact, correct?

19:28.900 --> 19:34.270
If we could collapse the Passageway, why haven't we done it sooner?!

19:34.870 --> 19:37.270
Because we got greedy.

19:39.010 --> 19:41.270
Hey! What's that giant... thing?!

19:45.610 --> 19:48.020
Think about it.

19:48.020 --> 19:51.750
Humanity saw unknown dimensions for the first time.

19:51.750 --> 19:54.820
Resources. An entire star system.

19:54.820 --> 19:59.350
It was all just too much to resist.

20:02.500 --> 20:05.120
But, even that...

20:06.070 --> 20:11.020
It seems it was all a mirage, manufactured by the JAM.

20:19.810 --> 20:24.820
There's no reason left for us to remain here.

20:24.820 --> 20:32.120
It's possible that the entire planet itself is the JAM.

20:32.560 --> 20:34.360
Pardon me.

20:34.360 --> 20:36.170
Phone call for the brigadier.

20:38.300 --> 20:40.320
Yes, speaking.

20:41.800 --> 20:42.960
To Yukikaze?!

20:43.240 --> 20:47.030
Yes, ma'am. They put a squad of MPs around it right after it landed.

20:43.670 --> 20:49.420
<i>18th maintainance group, resupply all units of 128TAS.</i>

20:47.040 --> 20:48.050
Right.

20:48.070 --> 20:51.240
They're not even letting my maintainance crew near it.

20:49.550 --> 20:55.740
<i>Repeat. 18th maintainance group, resupply all units of 128TAS.</i>

20:52.380 --> 20:55.740
Right, it's completely locked down.

20:58.050 --> 21:03.990
So, at the very least, you can take the data B-3 has on the JAM back to Earth.

21:04.430 --> 21:07.280
Is that what you're planning, Sir?

21:08.100 --> 21:11.000
That is my duty.

21:11.000 --> 21:19.060
We must bring that data back safely if we're to honor all those who died here.

21:27.720 --> 21:30.320
<i>Nord 20, resupply, complete.</i>

21:30.410 --> 21:34.480
<i>526TFS flight officers, please report to maintainance command.</i>

21:34.790 --> 21:40.920
<i>Repeat. 526TFS flight officers, please report to maintainance command.</i>

21:43.960 --> 21:46.570
Figured I'd find you here.

21:46.590 --> 21:49.870
<i>Transferring Harpy 05 to hanger.</i>

21:48.400 --> 21:53.580
I've been running around all over, asking people "Just service it, please!"

21:49.870 --> 21:54.920
<i>Maintainance group 6, once work is complete, resupply Ceres 15.</i>

21:53.600 --> 21:55.910
No one was willing to help me.

21:55.250 --> 22:01.340
<i>Repeat. Maintainance group 6, once work is complete, resupply Ceres 15.</i>

22:04.750 --> 22:07.400
How about getting some rest?

22:06.950 --> 22:13.360
<i>SAF unit 8, Jillvette, cleared for imminent landing.</i>

22:13.360 --> 22:17.100
See you. And don't worry about Yukikaze.

22:13.360 --> 22:16.710
<i>Flight officer should report to LSO deck ASAP.</i>

22:17.100 --> 22:20.350
We'll bring you both home safely.

22:17.100 --> 22:21.360
<i>Repeat. Flight officer should report to LSO deck ASAP.</i>

22:30.440 --> 22:33.740
<i>We've just now finished taking the crew from Valkia base aboard.</i>

22:33.750 --> 22:35.920
<i>Reception from both bases is complete.</i>

22:35.920 --> 22:37.980
<i>Closing protection gate.</i>

22:48.630 --> 22:49.570
This is the one.

22:54.030 --> 22:55.290
He's dead.

22:55.330 --> 22:56.970
Nasty...

22:59.700 --> 23:03.150
Okay, next one. Block C-5!

23:09.580 --> 23:11.770
What's the condition of B-3?

23:11.950 --> 23:14.090
No change.

23:14.090 --> 23:16.790
It's scanning the remaining copies aboard.

23:17.630 --> 23:21.190
Yukikaze is continuing to fight.

23:22.730 --> 23:29.600
If Capt. Foss's analysis is correct and a major JAM invasion is the outcome, then...

23:32.770 --> 23:36.180
Contact the major! Do it now!

23:39.180 --> 23:41.280
<i>B-4, Zook, to Banshee.</i>

23:41.280 --> 23:44.480
<i>A large number of JAM have appeared near Sugar Rock.</i>

23:44.480 --> 23:48.480
<i>It's a huge number. Too many blips for my monitor to resolve.</i>

23:48.480 --> 23:53.240
Use Yukikaze?! But, ma'am...

23:53.290 --> 23:55.870
We have no other choice now!

23:56.660 --> 23:59.940
<i>Those people don't understand the situation at all!</i>

24:00.160 --> 24:05.130
<i>Or the reason the JAM keep making the combat intelligence so interesting to them!</i>

24:05.140 --> 24:08.810
<i>ASA341, climb to 17000 and hold.</i>

24:06.770 --> 24:12.040
Do you see? The JAM's prime targets are Lt. Fukai and Yukikaze!

24:08.810 --> 24:12.040
<i>Maintain heading until we reach area 7-7.</i>

24:13.810 --> 24:17.540
<i>There's no way they'd allow them to escape to Earth under their very noses!</i>

24:17.820 --> 24:21.420
<i>I'm ordering them to sortie on my authority.</i>

24:21.580 --> 24:24.150
<i>I'm counting on you, Major.</i>

24:31.270 --> 24:33.150
<i>B-7, Ranvabon, to Banshee.</i>

24:33.500 --> 24:37.410
<i>Large numbers of booster-types spotted. It's too many to count.</i>

24:38.440 --> 24:40.830
<i>It looks like a carnival...</i>

24:42.180 --> 24:44.920
Range to Passageway now 700 kilometers!

24:45.010 --> 24:48.180
All fighters have formed up completely around this ship.

24:48.550 --> 24:52.460
Our outer escort line is composed of our unmanned fighter unit.

24:53.250 --> 24:55.970
It's just a matter of time before they make contact.

24:56.590 --> 24:58.930
All ships, go to DefCon 1.

24:58.930 --> 25:01.400
All ships, sound DefCon 1!

25:00.740 --> 25:04.160
Now switching mode to
combat sortie status.

25:01.850 --> 25:04.160
Secure bulkheads
throughout the ship!

25:04.160 --> 25:06.980
All hands, prep to repel airborne attack!

25:07.000 --> 25:10.940
<i>Fire suppression teams, to your stations.</i>

25:11.100 --> 25:14.980
<i>Those without specific orders are not to move throughout the ship.</i>

25:14.980 --> 25:18.500
<i>Repeat. Ship is now at DefCon 1.</i>

25:25.920 --> 25:31.130
<i>Carrier 1, hold to the rear of Banshee 3. Maintain course and position until further notice.</i>

25:31.130 --> 25:35.760
<i>411WW. All gunships, form up around carrier 1 and provide escort.</i>

25:35.760 --> 25:38.500
<i>411WW. All gunships, form up around carrier 1...</i>

25:38.500 --> 25:43.900
All combat units, maintain formation
and patrol assigned areas.

25:41.870 --> 25:43.900
We're babysitting
the bombs, huh?

25:44.010 --> 25:50.600
<i>Repeat. All combat units, maintain formation and patrol assigned areas.</i>

25:50.640 --> 25:54.720
<i>526TFS, Ghoul 2 and 4, launch from upper deck!</i>

25:54.920 --> 25:58.050
Ghoul 7 and 8,
launch from lower deck.

25:56.720 --> 26:00.650
505TFS, all units, move ahead of us
and prep for forward intercept.

25:58.050 --> 26:00.650
Roger, Banshee 3.
This is Ghoul leader.

26:00.650 --> 26:02.260
<i>Ghoul 5 to flight deck.</i>

26:02.260 --> 26:05.290
<i>Once shield door is open, ramp out Nord 22.</i>

26:05.290 --> 26:07.800
<i>Nord 17, resupply, complete.</i>

26:07.800 --> 26:10.230
<i>Nord 17, ramp out.</i>

26:10.230 --> 26:13.750
<i>Maintainance crews, report to assigned blocks at once!</i>

26:27.280 --> 26:30.020
Take Yukikaze out.

26:37.020 --> 26:39.490
You just stand without a word?

26:41.260 --> 26:42.620
<i>It's begun.</i>

26:43.830 --> 26:48.400
<i>505TFS unmanned units have contacted the leading edge of the JAM.</i>

26:48.400 --> 26:49.790
<i>Engaging.</i>

27:04.650 --> 27:06.340
Do you understand?

27:07.450 --> 27:10.420
They're after you and Yukikaze!

27:11.230 --> 27:14.320
All of the JAM are...

27:16.960 --> 27:20.690
If you go out into that, do you understand what will happen?!

27:43.460 --> 27:45.990
What the... They're suddenly!

27:45.990 --> 27:47.170
Hey, look!

27:47.430 --> 27:48.890
A new one...

27:49.600 --> 27:51.310
An electronic warfare type!

27:51.830 --> 27:54.270
B-12, Onyx, to Banshee!

27:54.270 --> 27:57.830
It's a new type of JAM! It's disrupting our unmanned units!

28:04.580 --> 28:07.580
Why? Why are you so calm?!

28:08.550 --> 28:11.830
Why do you have to go?!

28:13.590 --> 28:17.820
Or is it because... you're trying to be a hero?!

28:22.730 --> 28:25.430
Please let me go, Jack.

28:38.050 --> 28:43.450
I always knew you would say that.

28:53.630 --> 28:56.620
<i>Left turn... NOW!</i>

29:13.210 --> 29:14.890
<i>It's started over there, too!</i>

29:15.950 --> 29:18.140
<i>This gonna be a REALLY long day.</i>

29:18.320 --> 29:20.820
<i>Continue to engage with 327TFS.</i>

29:20.820 --> 29:26.930
412TFS and 185TFS, contact
the enemy vanguard and engage!

29:24.150 --> 29:26.930
Almost in visual range
of the Passageway.

29:26.930 --> 29:30.260
Main JAM forces are gathering in front of the Passageway.

29:50.440 --> 29:51.870
What the hell?

30:21.550 --> 30:26.380
All ships, prepare to intercept! First wave, approaching! Their numbers are enormous!

30:27.390 --> 30:28.610
They're fast...

30:29.860 --> 30:30.670
Here they come!

30:38.530 --> 30:41.940
<i>Ghoul 1 to all units! Form up in front and intercept!</i>

30:41.940 --> 30:44.930
<i>This is Ghoul 13! Formation two will backup formation one!</i>

30:51.840 --> 30:55.040
<i>That's it, just like that... BINGO!</i>

30:55.280 --> 30:59.160
<i>Ghoul leader, this is Ghoul 6!
I have three Type 1s on my tail!</i>

30:59.370 --> 31:01.880
<i>Shake 'em off, Ghoul 6! I'm on my way!</i>

31:02.220 --> 31:05.750
<i>Shit, I can't shake 'em! Help me!</i>

31:12.270 --> 31:14.570
Thanks for the save, SAF!

31:14.570 --> 31:15.840
<i>Godspeed!</i>

31:15.940 --> 31:19.310
You, too! I'll buy you a drink when we get back to Earth, Brother!

31:19.310 --> 31:21.150
<i>New contacts, bearing to starboard!</i>

31:21.150 --> 31:22.940
Roger! Starboard!

31:27.150 --> 31:29.550
All of it! Load it all on board!

31:29.550 --> 31:31.520
We've finished equipping the left generator!

31:31.520 --> 31:34.950
Leave the laser calibration for later! Get the harness strung first!

31:35.390 --> 31:37.660
Turbine fix, complete!

31:37.660 --> 31:42.420
The coupler won't fit? It was made for a Rafe. Well make it fit!

31:43.800 --> 31:46.470
Fleet now passing the outer edge of the Passageway.

31:47.830 --> 31:50.630
Carrier 1, moving ahead!

31:50.660 --> 31:52.140
Carrier 1, advance.

31:52.140 --> 31:56.510
Gunship units, take maximum defensive formation and escort it on the same course.

32:03.350 --> 32:04.610
<i>Shit!</i>

32:06.550 --> 32:07.750
<i>What?!</i>

32:09.630 --> 32:12.990
<i>Damned machine stole my kill!</i>

32:13.020 --> 32:15.620
Good luck, sir! Godspeed!

32:15.650 --> 32:17.130
We're counting on you!

32:39.190 --> 32:42.430
<i>All units, don't let 'em lay a finger on Carrier 1!</i>

32:45.430 --> 32:47.080
My radar just suddenly...

32:48.010 --> 32:48.770
What?!

32:55.040 --> 32:58.030
The Passageway's gone? Wha?!

33:02.110 --> 33:03.780
<i>All units, break off!</i>

33:03.780 --> 33:04.880
<i>No good!</i>

33:05.540 --> 33:08.590
<i>Emergency! Break off! I...</i>

33:08.610 --> 33:10.750
<i>That whole current is
nothing but JAM!</i>

33:09.350 --> 33:10.750
<i>GPS data, lost!</i>

33:10.750 --> 33:14.480
<i>My instruments! I can't tell
which way I'm headed!</i>

33:11.750 --> 33:14.480
<i>Banshee 3, give us
a bearing! Banshee!</i>

33:14.650 --> 33:18.570
It's a new type of JAM! We have to pull our fighters out of there!

33:18.660 --> 33:20.890
Y- You mean...

33:21.230 --> 33:23.490
All of that is?!

33:44.320 --> 33:47.330
<i>Please tell me, Rei.</i>

33:49.360 --> 33:54.920
<i>What sort of voice have you been hearing all this time?</i>

33:55.360 --> 34:00.290
<i>As you flew with a fairy in the skies of this world...</i>

34:04.800 --> 34:08.520
That's a JAM?! You gotta be kidding me!

34:09.880 --> 34:11.480
H- Hey!

34:14.980 --> 34:17.840
Banshee! Something's wrong with the unmanned planes!

34:35.800 --> 34:41.390
<i>That time before... Did you hear Yukikaze's voice, too?</i>

34:42.010 --> 34:45.520
<i>The voice of a fairy created only to fight?</i>

34:48.290 --> 34:52.690
<i>In the end, I didn't understand anything.</i>

34:55.890 --> 34:58.260
Should I fire all the Knight units?

34:58.260 --> 35:01.490
It's useless! In this situation...

35:02.400 --> 35:05.640
<i>Banshee, Carrier 1 has been hit!</i>

35:11.710 --> 35:13.410
Carrier 1, down!

35:13.410 --> 35:15.800
Emergency abort on the Flip Knight system!

35:17.040 --> 35:20.760
If the Knight unit auto-destructs, we'll be blown apart, too!

35:35.330 --> 35:36.230
Wha?!

35:36.490 --> 35:40.900
All the Knight units have separated from Carrier 1!
All of them are now uncontrolled!

35:41.840 --> 35:44.600
The warhead detonation timers have just activated!

35:44.970 --> 35:46.870
<i>Even so, Rei.</i>

35:47.410 --> 35:52.100
<i>I was always the one who sent you out to fly.</i>

35:58.920 --> 36:00.920
Is Knight flying autonomously?

36:00.920 --> 36:04.260
Um, no, sir. And it won't accept the emergency abort code!

36:04.260 --> 36:08.290
Hey! Don't release the lock on the protection gate! We're under attack!

36:08.290 --> 36:10.560
I'm not! The system's doing it by itself!

36:12.730 --> 36:15.210
It... It's being controlled externally!

36:15.770 --> 36:18.730
The Flip Knight's flying on external control!

36:18.970 --> 36:20.370
External?!

36:20.370 --> 36:22.340
The flight deck!

36:23.110 --> 36:26.840
One of the planes on board is opening the gate from inside!

36:37.320 --> 36:40.960
Let's go, Yukikaze.

37:13.390 --> 37:15.370
<i>Promise me you'll make it back.</i>

37:16.030 --> 37:19.920
<i>That's the one order I always give to you.</i>

37:20.700 --> 37:23.260
Who sent out B-3?!

37:23.470 --> 37:25.560
Is this Rombert's doing?

37:26.440 --> 37:28.510
Brigadier, was it you?!

37:29.680 --> 37:30.950
Yes, sir.

37:32.110 --> 37:37.730
Because I don't want to die without playing our strongest card.

37:38.220 --> 37:39.760
Our strongest?

37:40.190 --> 37:42.380
A composite life form.

37:44.260 --> 37:46.000
Machine and man.

37:48.390 --> 37:53.300
They recognize each other as completely different existences.

37:54.130 --> 37:59.160
Now seemingly fused together to a high degree to become a new life form.

38:19.790 --> 38:23.730
Exactly the way they are, now...

38:24.330 --> 38:25.240
<i>Bingo!</i>

38:25.240 --> 38:27.860
<i>Found 'em! All units, follow me!</i>

38:37.380 --> 38:39.000
<i>What's...?</i>

38:39.000 --> 38:42.250
<i>Fire control just switched itself on...</i>

38:42.820 --> 38:44.250
<i>B-3...?</i>

38:44.250 --> 38:45.990
<i>B-3's calling for backup!</i>

38:45.990 --> 38:47.630
<i>All units, fire all missiles!</i>

38:47.630 --> 38:49.510
<i>Hand off control to B-3!</i>

39:01.760 --> 39:04.400
Machine and man...

39:04.400 --> 39:06.260
Is that even possible?

39:07.470 --> 39:10.810
If it isn't, we're just going to be destroyed.

39:11.950 --> 39:15.380
But I think the basis for it...

39:16.420 --> 39:19.870
...lies in something very normal.

39:21.120 --> 39:22.450
<i>So, please...</i>

39:23.110 --> 39:25.960
<i>So, please... This time, too...</i>

40:05.530 --> 40:09.710
<i>You understand, Rei? Promise me.</i>

40:10.040 --> 40:13.130
Promise me you'll come back!

40:34.190 --> 40:35.700
Promise me.

40:51.820 --> 40:53.680
So, what happened to him?

40:53.680 --> 40:55.920
That's all I know.

40:56.120 --> 40:59.100
He vanished along with the Passageway.

40:59.690 --> 41:01.240
I see.

41:01.750 --> 41:03.330
Even so, the strange thing is...

41:04.620 --> 41:08.060
...I wasn't sad at all.

41:08.700 --> 41:12.140
No matter what, the idea that he died, well...

41:17.040 --> 41:18.780
I just don't buy it.

41:22.710 --> 41:27.950
He's somewhere out there, living a happy life.

41:27.950 --> 41:32.580
I just can't help but think that...

41:39.890 --> 41:42.500
<i>The hyperspace passageway was destroyed.</i>

41:42.500 --> 41:45.900
<i>The planet Fairy vanished from before our eyes.</i>

41:45.900 --> 41:48.630
<i>Along with the alien life forms we called JAM.</i>

41:50.640 --> 41:56.040
<i>Most of the FAF personnel were able to escape from Fairy.</i>

41:56.040 --> 42:01.860
<i>But the cost came with a huge number of those dead and missing.</i>

42:03.950 --> 42:06.090
<i>Yukikaze...</i>

42:06.090 --> 42:13.010
<i>That beautiful fighter plane and its pilot, Lt. Fukai, were among them.</i>

47:07.220 --> 47:09.170
Hold at high altitude.

47:09.170 --> 47:13.430
After that, you will search for the enemy from area two-niner to three-zero.

47:13.430 --> 47:16.460
All SAF units will carry out this mission.

47:16.490 --> 47:20.660
You've already been briefed on which sectors you'll each be responsible for.

47:20.670 --> 47:24.200
That's it. Today's briefing is over.

47:24.350 --> 47:26.810
And no matter how bad the situation may get,

47:27.110 --> 47:29.980
I want all planes to make it back here.

47:29.980 --> 47:32.410
That's an order.

47:32.410 --> 47:34.210
That's all. Dismissed.

47:47.030 --> 47:50.500
B-3, taking off.
